Now apply the same machinery to the derivative term. The derivative acts on the plane wave: $-\partial_x^2 e^{ipx}=p^2e^{ipx}.$ Therefore $\begin{aligned}
H_{\mathrm{kin}}
&=\int dx\,\psi^\dagger(x)
\left(-\frac{\partial_x^2}{2m}\right)\psi(x)\\
&=\int dp\,\frac{p^2}{2m}\,a^\dagger(p)a(p).
\end{aligned}$ Again the spatial integral enforces equal incoming and outgoing momentum. The new factor $p^2/2m$ simply weights the number of particles in each momentum mode by the kinetic energy of that mode.

